The IDE's gutter no longer marks a line verified while another member on that line is still waiting to be verified, or is being verified (https://github.com/erniecohen/dafny/issues/426). Each line took the highest status of the members on it, and a verified member's status is higher than a pending one's. So when, for example, a constructor and a method share a line, the line read verified as soon as the constructor verified, and went to failed only when the method failed, which in a large file could take most of the run. The line now reads verified-but-pending in that case, and verified once every member on it has verified.
